### Issue description

When DomainUpDown.Sorted is false, calling Items.Insert(index, item) at an index before or at the current selection index (index <= SelectedIndex) does not update the internal selection index (_domainIndex).

Because _domainIndex is not shifted:
1. SelectedIndex keeps its old numeric value, which now points to a different item in the collection.
2. SelectedItem returns the item at that index (the newly inserted or shifted item), while the Text property still reflects the previously selected item.
3. Clicking the up/down spin buttons or calling UpButton()/DownButton() navigates from the wrong item position.

In comparison, DomainUpDownItemCollection.RemoveAt(int index) already has logic to adjust _domainIndex when an item before or at _domainIndex is removed, but Insert was missing corresponding adjustment logic when Sorted is false.

### Steps to reproduce

```csharp
using var control = new DomainUpDown();
control.Items.AddRange(new string[] { "Item1", "Item2", "Item3" });
control.SelectedIndex = 1; // "Item2"

// Insert an item at index 0 (before SelectedIndex)
control.Items.Insert(0, "NewItem");

// Expected:
// SelectedIndex should be 2, pointing to "Item2"
// SelectedItem should be "Item2"
// Text should be "Item2"

// Actual:
// SelectedIndex is still 1
// SelectedItem is "NewItem"
// Text is "Item2"
```

